      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "FROSTNIP (5) is the one to beat on her Victorian form and has been fitted with two sharp trials. Showed good tactical speed in Vic, so expecting Moor to spear across from sticky draw and be prominent. Bold showing anticipated. URBAN LAD (8) led pillar-to-post to get off the mark here when resuming last campaign. Couldn't repeat the dose in her next two but it wasn't without trying. Strips fitter for two recent trials and gets in well at the weights with McColm's 3kg claim. Big threat. LIFE AFTER LOVE (10) is the race-fit danger, third at Doomben last start and now third-up with a reliable record at the distance. Thompson sticking is another good push. MERCATELLO (9) has to rebound from two plain Doomben runs, but her one start at this track produced a win and the return to 1100m gives her chance to return to the winner's circle.",
